      "updated": 1794942798187,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- tests that prove the contract holds (you can still GET /vendors/{id} and you still get teh same kind\nof data back, for example.)\n    - most of your discussion and design effort should be on the interface (the HTTP interface)\n- does it work\n- does it do the right thing\n    - usually system, but if there are too many paths, unit integration\n- does it do the thing right\n    - usually a unit test, or unit integration",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- tests that prove the contract holds (you can still GET /vendors/{id} and you still get teh same kind\nof data back, for example.)\n    - most of your discussion and design effort should be on the interface (the HTTP interface)\n- does it work\n- does it do the right thing\n    - usually system, but if there are too many paths, unit integration\n- does it do the thing right\n    - usually a unit test, or unit integration",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
